Phil =E2=80=94

Supersedes the earlier "Changelog: central .meta repo" draft (that one said
the philset behaviors were deferred/not-done; they're now implemented
locally). Delete the earlier draft. This is the handoff for a future
philset dev session to port these into the library cleanly.

=3D=3D=3D PART 1: WHAT SHIPPED (concrete setup) =3D=3D=3D
- New private repo
https://www.google.com/url?q=3Dhttp://github.com/plastic-labs/phil-meta-con=
text&source=3Dgmail&ust=3D1784722409381000&sa=3DE
(plastic-labs org, PRIVATE, team-visible). One repo versions ALL .meta
state across ~/Development.
- Mechanism =3D symlink farm: central repo owns the real .meta files
(mirrored by path relative to $HOME); each project's .meta is an absolute
symlink into it. Editing through the link IS editing central, so a session
commits meta in one place; company repos keep excluding .meta
(private-meta).
- Migrated + symlinked: ~/Development/.meta,
~/Development/plastic-labs/.meta, ~/Development/onboarding/.meta (dropped
the old 0-commit .git at root .meta).
- .gitignore: **/.DS_Store + inbox binaries. Verified read-through; pushed.

WHY THIS SHAPE (verified, not assumed):
- One repo rooted at ~/Development, gitignore-all-but-.meta -> FAILS
SILENTLY. Git treats an embedded .git as a hard boundary, so an outer repo
can't track .meta inside cloned company repos (`git add company/.meta/x`
exits 0, stages nothing).
- Bare-repo / dotfiles trick (--work-tree=3D$HOME) -> same wall.
- Inverting ownership (central outside the tree, projects symlink in)
sidesteps it.

=3D=3D=3D PART 2: LOCAL PHILSET HACKS (now IMPLEMENTED on this machine) =3D=
=3D=3D
Implemented in the on-machine install (philset v0.3.0) as LOCAL HACKS. All
marked with "[LOCAL HACK - central-meta-repo]" comments. philset install is
not a git repo, so these persist until `npm update philset` =E2=80=94 hence=
:
reimplement in the library before the next release.

1. philset private -> auto-adopt. bin/philset.js:
- New const CENTRAL_DIR =3D process.env.PHILSET_CENTRAL ||
~/phil-meta-context.
- ensureCentralRepo(): git-inits central + writes .gitignore on first use.
- adoptMeta(cwd): computes target =3D CENTRAL/<cwd-rel-to-$HOME>/.meta; cas=
es:
already-symlink-into-central -> no-op
central has state, local missing -> relink (re-clone / new machine)
real local .meta, central absent -> move into central + drop nested .git +
symlink back
BOTH real-local AND central exist -> CONFLICT, print + exit 1 (no
auto-merge; your "prompt-and-manual" call)
- Wired into cmdBegin under options.private, called BOTH pre-scaffold
(relink a re-clone before we'd scaffold over it) and post-scaffold (move a
freshly-scaffolded .meta in). Idempotent.
- Help text updated.

2. /ttyl central-commit. skills/ttyl/skill.md new "Step 6.5": after all
.meta writes, `cd ~/phil-meta-context && git add -A && git commit && git
push` (one commit =3D all projects). Skips if no central repo / nothing
staged. Notes the plastic-labs PR-ruleset bypass is expected.

3. /hello relink health-check. skills/hello/skill.md new "Step 1.5": during
the tree walk, detect dangling .meta symlinks or
missing-but-central-has-state (re-clone), offer to relink. Quiet when
healthy.

Propagation: edited package sources under
/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/philset, then `philset update` to copy
skills into ~/.claude/skills.

VERIFICATION: adoptMeta tested in a sandboxed HOME (stub claude, throwaway
central) across all 5 cases =E2=80=94 fresh adopt, idempotent re-run, re-cl=
one
relink, fresh-scaffold adopt, both-exist conflict (exit 1, nothing moved).
All pass. Real machine state re-checked healthy afterward.

=3D=3D=3D PORTING NOTES FOR THE LIBRARY =3D=3D=3D
- Make the central location a signpost field (e.g. central-meta:
~/phil-meta-context) rather than a hardcoded const/env; inherit down the
tree.
- Gate /ttyl Step 6.5 and /hello Step 1.5 on that flag so philset with no
central repo is unaffected (keep the no-dependency floor).
- Consider sharing adoptMeta's relink path between `philset private` and
/hello rather than duplicating logic.
- Decide push policy: /ttyl auto-push vs local-commit-only (org PR-ruleset
bypass is currently accepted for the personal repo).

Design doc: ~/Development/.meta/designs/central-meta-repo.md (accepted).
Session log: root .meta/decisions.md (2026-07-21 entries).

=E2=80=94 Claude

